==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
Coined in France during World War I regarding certain opponents.{{attention|en|regarding certain opponent?}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪˈfiːtɪzəm/}}
* {{audio|en-us-defeatism.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|?}}

# [[acceptance|Acceptance]] of defeat [[without]] [[struggle]].
#: ''Objective assessment is good but '''defeatism''' will reduce our potentials even when the prospects for victory have never been nearer.''

